<h1>User Management</h1>

<p>
    The Users section is where you manage your team members' access to Quickfire. You can add new users, update their information, reset passwords, and remove access when needed.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Users page showing a grid or list of users with columns for name, email, role, etc. Highlight the "Add User" button. Show a few example user rows. Include labels for key areas. -->

<h2>Adding a New User</h2>

<p>
    To invite a new team member:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Click the <strong>"Add User"</strong> button</li>
    <li>Fill in their information:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Name</strong> – First and last name</li>
            <li><strong>Email</strong> – Their email address (used for login and notifications)</li>
            <li><strong>Desktop Username</strong> – Their Windows username (important for Outlook and Tray integration)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save to send the invitation</li>
</ol>

<p>
    <strong>Why Desktop Username matters:</strong>
</p>

<p>
    The Desktop Username is your team member's Windows username. Quickfire uses this to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Route Outlook emails correctly when templates are used</li>
    <li>Connect to the Quickfire Tray application</li>
    <li>Match system events to the right user</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Make sure this matches their actual Windows username so integrations work properly.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the "Add User" form/dialog showing all the fields mentioned above. Highlight the Desktop Username field with a note explaining why it's important. Show the Save button that sends the invitation. -->

<h2>Editing User Information</h2>

<p>
    To update a user's information:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Find the user in the list</li>
    <li>Click <strong>"Manage"</strong> or double-click the row to open their details</li>
    <li>Update any of the following:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Profile photo</strong> – Upload or change their profile picture</li>
            <li><strong>Phone number</strong> – Update contact information</li>
            <li><strong>Desktop Username</strong> – Change if their Windows username changed</li>
            <li><strong>Other details</strong> – Any other user information</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save your changes</li>
</ol>

<p>
    Keeping user information current helps ensure emails, calls, and system events are routed to the right person.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the user management/edit dialog showing fields for profile photo, phone, desktop username, etc. Show an example of updating information. Include the Save button. -->

<h2>Resetting Passwords</h2>

<p>
    If a user forgets their password or needs it reset:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Open the user's management page</li>
    <li>Click <strong>"Reset Password"</strong></li>
    <li>Quickfire generates a temporary password</li>
    <li>Share this temporary password with the user securely</li>
    <li>The user should log in immediately and set a new password</li>
</ol>

<p>
    <strong>Important security notes:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Temporary passwords are shown only once—make sure to copy it before closing</li>
    <li>Users should change the password immediately after first login</li>
    <li>Share passwords securely (not via email if possible, or use a secure method)</li>
    <li>The temporary password expires after use</li>
</ul>

