<h2>User Roles and Permissions</h2>

<p>
    Users can have different roles that determine what they can access and do in Quickfire. Common roles include:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Administrator</strong> – Full access to all features and settings</li>
    <li><strong>Agent/CSR</strong> – Standard user access for daily work</li>
    <li><strong>Read-only</strong> – Can view but not edit (if applicable)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    Roles are typically set when creating the user, but can be changed later if needed. Check with your system administrator about what roles are available in your Quickfire setup.
</p>

